       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That's twice the usual maximum of 2,550 mg/day (2,000 mg/day for extended-release). A single 1,700 mg dose is also twice the usual maximum single dose of 850 mg. At this level the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity goes up substantially, even with normal renal and hepatic function.\n\nWhich of these did you mean?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day), which may be what you intended.\n- **1700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg PO twice daily with meals.\n- **1700 mg PO three times daily**, if the dose is intentional. Please confirm it and I'll enter it with a note documenting the override.\n\nOnce you confirm, I'll enter the order."
      }
